  1. Vulnerability analysis of Vault ERC-4626 lending shares
     Priority: 9 | Impact: high | Category: aspect
     Reasoning: WHY NOW: V3Vault and its operational modules have been analyzed,
but the lending-share accounting layer remains a distinct high-value component 
that determines lender ownership and claim amounts. ERC-4626 rounding, 
unsolicited-token handling, and synchronization with vault debt or reserves can 
create dilution, insolvency, or withdrawal denial even when borrowing and 
liquidation logic is otherwise correct. EXIT CRITERIA: Trace every share 
issuance and burn path, derive the conversion formulas under empty, donated, 
loss, debt-accrual, and liquidation states, verify rounding cannot create value 
or strand assets, confirm all ERC-4626 entry points preserve accounting 
invariants and authorization expectations, and document any exploitable mismatch
or conclude that lender-share balances remain solvent and consistent with vault 
assets and liabilities.

